    <deps>020</deps>
    <blocks>060</blocks>
    <tags>bff-api, communication</tags>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies the shared `AssociationStatusMapper`/`AutoFileGate` that decides auto-file vs `Suggested` for EVERY association. Narrowing to rung 0+1 is a policy tightening (ADR-045 path-A exception) — a mistake here either auto-files a weak match (misfile, #1 trust-killer) or blocks a legitimate auto-file. BFF-touching + `.cs` in the shared engine → code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5; publish-size + CVE + `/conflict-check` required.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>P2-assoc</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>A well-specified policy narrowing over an existing mapper/gate (rung-level threshold change + Suggested fallback) — clear rules, no open-ended design. Default execution tier at `high` effort for correctness on a shared-path edit.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <fr-refs>FR-03</fr-refs>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Narrow the shipped auto-file policy to C-1 in the EXISTING `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/AssociationStatusMapper.cs` + `AutoFileGate.cs`. Today the engine auto-files deterministic matches at rungs 0–3 (≥0.85). C-1 tightens this: **auto-file ONLY on rung 0 (explicit ID) + rung 1 (thread inheritance); rung 2 (participant/sender-only) and rung 3 (structural) resolve to `Suggested`, never auto-file.** This is a documented ADR-045 path-A exception (misfiling = #1 trust-killer) — a tightening of the shipped policy, kill-switch-governed, not a new mechanism.

    Additionally honor the identifier rung's (020) reinforcement signal: a **bare-numeric identifier match with NO reinforcement MUST resolve to `Suggested`**, not auto-file — even though the identifier rung is rung-0-class, a bare-numeric-only token is not a strong-enough explicit match to auto-file alone. Consume the rung-level + reinforcement flag that task 020's rung emits.

    Do NOT change the rung ORDER or the rung matching logic (that is 020) — this task changes only the STATUS MAPPING: which rung levels/results map to `auto-file` vs `Suggested`. Keep the AI-tier rule intact (AI-tier never auto-files). Add/extend tests proving the narrowed policy. Keep the change kill-switch-governed (ADR-018) so the policy can be toggled without a redeploy if needed.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer for the Communication Association Engine — authority on `AssociationStatusMapper`/`AutoFileGate` (the auto-file-vs-Suggested decision). Fluent in ADR-045 (the shipped auto-file policy + the C-1 path-A tightening), ADR-018 (kill-switch governance), the rung ladder's level/reinforcement contract from task 020, §10 BFF Hygiene, and §11. You change only the status-mapping policy, not the matching logic, and you never let a weak match auto-file.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `AssociationStatusMapper`/`AutoFileGate` auto-file ONLY on rung 0 + rung 1; rung 2 + rung 3 resolve to `Suggested`. A bare-numeric identifier match with no reinforcement resolves to `Suggested` (consuming 020's reinforcement flag). AI-tier never auto-files (unchanged). The narrowing is kill-switch-governed. Build clean; tests prove: thread-reply (rung 1) and explicit-well-formed-ID (rung 0) auto-file; sender-only (rung 2) and structural (rung 3) land `Suggested`; bare-numeric-only lands `Suggested`. Existing association tests updated to the new policy and green; publish-size delta ≈0 + no new HIGH CVE; `/conflict-check` run before the PR.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      ADR-045 ships auto-file for deterministic matches at rungs 0–3 (≥0.85). Design research found misfiling is the #1 trust-killer, so C-1 conservatively narrows auto-file to the two rungs that carry the strongest intent: rung 0 (explicit identifier) + rung 1 (thread inheritance). Rung 2 (participant/sender-only) and rung 3 (structural) still MATCH but resolve to `Suggested` for human confirmation. This is a documented ADR-045 path-A exception (a tightening, kill-switch-governed — not a violation, not a new mechanism); it is recorded in the spec/plan ADR-Tensions tables.

      The identifier rung (020) adds a subtlety: a bare-numeric token is rung-0-class by KIND but is weak by itself (a number with no sender/participant/thread reinforcement could match coincidentally). So the policy also treats bare-numeric-without-reinforcement as `Suggested`, consuming the reinforcement flag 020 emits. This task is pure policy: it changes which rung levels/results map to auto-file — it does NOT touch the matching logic.

      §11: this task ONLY modifies existing files (`AssociationStatusMapper`/`AutoFileGate`) — no new surface; no §11 three-question form required (the rule applies to NEW surface). The change is a policy narrowing + a consumed reinforcement flag.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/AssociationStatusMapper.cs (the rung-level → status mapping — narrow to rung 0+1 auto-file)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/AutoFileGate.cs (the auto-file gate — honor the C-1 narrowing + the bare-numeric reinforcement flag)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/Rungs/ (rung 0/1/2/3 — the levels the mapper keys on; task 020's identifier rung emits the reinforcement flag)</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/notes/ (task 020's note — the reinforcement-signal contract this task consumes)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-03 / C-1">Scope: auto-file ONLY on rung 0 + rung 1; rung 2 (participant/sender-only) and rung 3 (structural) → `Suggested`. A sender-only or structural-only match NEVER auto-files; a thread reply or explicit-ID match does.</constraint>
    <constraint source="C-1 (bare-numeric)">Scope: a bare-numeric identifier match with NO reinforcement → `Suggested`, not auto-file (consume 020's reinforcement flag). Bare-numeric alone never auto-files.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045 (path-A exception)">Scope: this is a documented tightening of the shipped auto-file policy, not a new mechanism. Change only the status mapping; MUST NOT alter the rung ORDER or matching logic (that is 020). Keep the AI-tier rule intact (AI-tier never auto-files).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-018">Scope: keep the narrowing kill-switch-governed so the policy can be toggled without a redeploy; do NOT hardwire a policy that cannot be reverted.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04">Scope: the status mapping MUST be best-effort — a mapping edge case degrades to `Suggested` (safe), never throws into the capture/enrichment path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project §10">Scope: BFF Hygiene — load `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; state the Placement Justification in the PR (policy narrowing of the existing mapper/gate — no new surface); report publish-size delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (expected ≈0); no new HIGH CVE; update tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/`; `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/Engine/`).</constraint>
  </constraints>

