  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` + the spec/plan ADR-Tensions (ADR-045 path-A) + task 020's note (the reinforcement-signal contract) before editing.</step>
    <step order="2">Read `AssociationStatusMapper.cs` + `AutoFileGate.cs` to fix exactly where rung level → auto-file/Suggested is decided, how the AI-tier rule is expressed, and where the kill-switch is read; confirm 020's rung emits the reinforcement flag this task consumes.</step>
    <step order="3">Characterize the current policy with a green baseline (record which rung levels auto-file today) so the narrowing is a deliberate, tested change.</step>
    <step order="4">Narrow the policy: auto-file only on rung 0 + rung 1; rung 2 + rung 3 → `Suggested`; bare-numeric-without-reinforcement → `Suggested` (consume 020's flag); AI-tier never auto-files (unchanged); keep it kill-switch-governed; best-effort (edge case → `Suggested`).</step>
    <step order="5">Update/add tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/`: (a) rung 1 thread reply auto-files; (b) rung 0 explicit well-formed ID auto-files; (c) NEGATIVE — rung 2 sender-only lands `Suggested`; (d) NEGATIVE — rung 3 structural lands `Suggested`; (e) NEGATIVE — bare-numeric-only (no reinforcement) lands `Suggested`; (f) AI-tier never auto-files; (g) the kill-switch toggles the policy. Update existing policy tests to the narrowed behavior.</step>
    <step order="6">Run `dotnet build` + `dotnet test --filter Communication`; confirm existing association tests reflect the new policy and pass.</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release ... -o deploy/api-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (expected ≈0).</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVEs.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` (focus: only status mapping changed not matching logic; rung 0+1-only auto-file; bare-numeric→Suggested; AI-tier unchanged; kill-switch present); `adr-check` (FR-03, ADR-045 path-A exception cited, ADR-018). Address Critical findings; cite the path-A exception in the PR.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/Engine/`; serial after 020 — never concurrent with 010/020).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (021 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record the rung levels that now auto-file + the kill-switch key.</step>
  </steps>

